# This module's Go sources are LF in the index and must be LF in the worktree
# too. gofmt compares the bytes ON DISK, so a CRLF checkout makes `gofmt -l`
# list a file that is byte-identical to a clean one. Measured here on
# providers.go: gofmt listed it, the file had CRLF endings, and CI on Linux
# passed green — a false positive that costs a diagnosis every time it fires.
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf=true, which is what put the CRLF there.
*.go text eol=lf

# There is no Git LFS rule any more. The vendored CLI binary
# (bin/retraction-checker-pp-cli-linux) was the only LFS-tracked file; the
# image now builds the CLI from a pinned upstream commit (see the Dockerfile),
# so the binary and vendor-cli.sh were removed. pubvera-bibliovera builds the
# same CLI from the same kind of pin, so no copy of it is kept in either
# repository. The old blobs and LFS objects stay in the history: removing
# those means rewriting history, which invalidates every existing clone and
# commit hash. That is a separate decision.